From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jaydens-tasty-slop
 <325336397+jaydens-tasty-slop@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 19:45:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/mdp5: no async plane updates on command-mode CRTCs

A command-mode panel gets a frame each time the CTL is started. The
regular commit path waits for the previous transfer's PP_DONE before it
flushes and starts again (mdp5_wait_flush()). The async plane path,
taken for legacy cursor moves, writes the pipe, flushes and starts right
away, so it can start a transfer while the previous one still runs.

Seen on the Samsung Galaxy Tab S3 (APQ8096, bonded command-mode DSI):
moving the X hardware cursor gave DSI FIFO and MDP FIFO underflow errors
(dsi_err_worker status 0xc and 0xd), "pp done time out", a garbled
picture and finally a dead panel until the next modeset. Refuse the fast
path on command-mode CRTCs, so cursor moves take a regular commit. With
this, 300 cursor moves across both halves of the panel gave no errors.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
index 841f444a8d..0341f56237 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/disp/mdp5/mdp5_plane.c
@@ -380,6 +380,15 @@ static int mdp5_plane_atomic_async_check(struct drm_plane *plane,
 	if (!crtc_state->active)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
+	/*
+	 * A command-mode panel gets a frame each time the CTL is started.
+	 * The fast path flushes and starts right away, possibly while the
+	 * previous transfer still runs; a regular commit waits for its
+	 * PP_DONE first.
+	 */
+	if (to_mdp5_crtc_state(crtc_state)->cmd_mode)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	/* don't use fast path if we don't have a hwpipe allocated yet */
 	if (!mdp5_state->hwpipe)
 		return -EINVAL;
